; Belisarius bli-micro.per — Prompt 7 PRACTICAL MICRO (high-impact only).
; Only behaviors the engine executes consistently (§61): siege protection,
; cavalry raid preservation is handled by stance (scouts never suicide into
; the main fight), monk value via targeting priorities (set once in init).
; No pixel-micro, no per-unit dance logic that would destabilize execution.

; Siege must not sit under cavalry: pull mangonels back to the shop when the
; enemy is inside and the screen is gone.
(defrule
  (up-compare-goal bli-enemy-in-town == bli-yes)
  (unit-type-count-total mangonel-line >= 1)
  (building-type-count-total siege-workshop >= 1)
  (unit-type-count-total spearman-line <= 0)
  (unit-type-count-total knight-line <= 0)
=>
  (up-retreat-to siege-workshop c: mangonel-line))
; Monks have no business forward without an escort: pull them to the town
; center when the enemy is inside and no army covers them.
(defrule
  (up-compare-goal bli-enemy-in-town == bli-yes)
  (unit-type-count-total monk >= 1)
  (building-type-count-total town-center >= 1)
  (military-population < 5)
=>
  (up-retreat-to town-center c: monk))
